A||||2||Eric||Good Autocross Today||||1||
Z||000000||Eric||05-20-2001||07:57 PM||||Today was the first points event for the OVR chapter of the SCCA.  I didn't catch any forum members out there, but there were two other Fieros.  One was a 86 SE V6, and the other was another V6 coupe in rough shape.  Both drivers were using race tires.  I was able to beat the coupe by a good 3 seconds.  The SE was a second faster than me at his best.  That car had a Belltech suspension and was quite a bit lower than my 88.<P>It's frustrating trying to deal with these Miatas.  I hate them.  They're all over the place for one thing, and they're, more often than not, driven well.  Half of CSP is Miata.  <P>I really am starting to learn how to drive my car even though I'm not exactly competitive.  Even "experienced" drivers don't run fast times the first time they come out, so I just try to concentrate on bettering my own timeslips.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||cadaver||05-20-2001||10:51 PM||||That is very cool. Maybe one day I will have a car I can cross. Just keep shaving those seconds.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||05-21-2001||08:30 AM||||I'm not sure when I'll make it out again.  I want to install my Dickman steering rack bushing before I race again.  But congratulations anyway.||||reg||1
